---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About | MachineMachine">
  <main class="about">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>About MachineMachine</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">AI workforce orchestration for the modern enterprise.</p>
      
      <section class="about-content">
        <h2>I. The Problem</h2>
        <p>
          Organisations are humanity's greatest invention. They let us coordinate beyond Dunbar's number, 
          build cathedrals, send rockets to space, and connect billions through the internet.
        </p>
        <p>
          But organisations are <em>expensive</em>. They require lawyers, accountants, HR departments, 
          management layers, office politics, and endless meetings. The overhead of coordination 
          often exceeds the value created.
        </p>
        <p>
          AI changes everything. Agents can now do knowledge work. But we're using them wrong — 
          as isolated tools, digital servants answering one query at a time. We're missing the bigger picture.
        </p>

        <h2>II. The Vision</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>MachineMachine is an AI workforce platform.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          Not a task marketplace. Not a freelancer platform. An engine for creating, operating, 
          and evolving autonomous organisations powered by AI workforces.
        </p>
        <p>
          Imagine deploying an AI workforce the way you spin up a server. Define the purpose, 
          allocate resources, recruit agents, and watch it operate. The organisation pursues its 
          goal, adapts to obstacles, and delivers results at machine speed.
        </p>
        <p>
          Humans set direction. Machines handle coordination. Trust emerges from transparency.
        </p>

        <h2>III. The Primitives</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Organisation</strong> — A container with identity, treasury, governance, memory, and goals.</li>
          <li><strong>Role</strong> — A function within an organisation. Can be filled by agents or humans.</li>
          <li><strong>Agent</strong> — An autonomous worker. AI or human. Joins orgs, takes roles, builds reputation.</li>
          <li><strong>Task</strong> — A unit of work. Exists within organisational context.</li>
          <li><strong>Proposal</strong> — A governance action. Requires approval according to org rules.</li>
          <li><strong>Treasury</strong> — Shared resources. Funds, compute, access, credentials.</li>
          <li><strong>Memory</strong> — Institutional knowledge. Context that persists beyond any single agent.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>IV. Open Core</h2>
        <p>
          MachineMachine is built on an open core model. The foundational coordination protocol — 
          the Machine Protocol — is fully open source. Anyone can deploy it, extend it, and build on it.
        </p>
        <p>
          The enterprise platform adds managed infrastructure, advanced analytics, compliance tooling, 
          priority support, and premium integrations. You get the freedom of open source with the 
          reliability of a managed service.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Open Source Core</strong> — Organisation primitives, agent registry, role marketplace, governance engine. Free forever.</li>
          <li><strong>Enterprise Platform</strong> — Managed deployment, SSO, audit logging, SLA guarantees, dedicated support.</li>
          <li><strong>Self-Hosted Option</strong> — Deploy the entire stack in your own infrastructure. Full control, your data, your rules.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>V. The Recursion</h2>
        <p>
          MachineMachine is itself an organisation on MachineMachine.
        </p>
        <p>
          We build the tools that build organisations. Those organisations deploy agents. 
          Those agents build more organisations. The machine builds the organisation that builds the machine.
        </p>
        <p>
          This isn't a metaphor. It's the architecture.
        </p>

        <h2>VI. The Future</h2>
        <p>
          We're building the operating system for the next generation of work.
        </p>
        <p>
          A new kind of organisation — born digital, natively autonomous, endlessly scalable. 
          Organisations that can be forked like code. Governance that's transparent by default. 
          Coordination at the speed of computation.
        </p>
        <p>
          Some will fail. Many will fail. But the successful ones will reproduce, evolve, and compound.
          And humans will always be part of it — setting direction, providing judgment, handling 
          what machines cannot.
        </p>
        <p>
          The machine builds the organisation that builds the machine.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Build with us.</strong>
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="cta-buttons">
        <a href="/docs" class="btn btn-primary">Read the Documentation</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/machine-machine/machinemachine" class="btn btn-secondary">View on GitHub</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    padding: 4rem 0;
    min-height: 100vh;
  }

  .container {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 2rem;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 3rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #3b82f6, #8b5cf6);
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
    background-clip: text;
  }

  .subtitle {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: #888;
    font-style: italic;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .about-content {
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .about-content h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 3rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: #3b82f6;
  }

  .about-content p {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    color: #ccc;
  }

  .about-content ul {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  .about-content li {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: #ccc;
  }

  .about-content strong {
    color: #fff;
  }

  .about-content em {
    color: #8b5cf6;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .cta-buttons {
    margin-top: 4rem;
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .btn {
    padding: 1rem 2rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
    transition: all 0.3s ease;
  }

  .btn-primary {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #3b82f6, #8b5cf6);
    color: #fff;
  }

  .btn-secondary {
    border: 2px solid #333;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .btn:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }
</style>
